  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A dark rocky moon locked to its planet and orbiting close to the plane, so that it eclipses the star from the dusk belt for about forty minutes every twenty-one days. Its surface is basalt and regolith with no ice at any latitude. It is lifeless, and its significance is entirely that the eclipse it causes is the only regular event visible from the ground on a world where nothing else in the sky moves.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
